{"name":"Oh Pistachio","hex":"#abca99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pistachio","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deciduous tree (Pistacia vera) grown in parts of Asia for its drupaceous fruit.","The nutlike fruit of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pistachio"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pistachio","blocks":[{"text":"The pistachio is a small to medium-sized tree of the cashew family. The tree produces seeds that are widely consumed as food. Pistachios can be used as an ingredient in desserts, chocolate, candy, ice cream, and as a paste or butter. As a tree nut, pistachios are considered a priority allergen that may induce allergic reactions in susceptible people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Pistachio_vera.jpg/330px-Pistachio_vera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pistachio","wikidata":"Q36071"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse","wikidata":"Q105563495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg/500px-860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg/1280px-860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb